  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nAlthough mostly cloudy conditions will persist as a shortwave \napproaches from the west, high pressure and dry air lingering \nin the low-levels are expected to maintain dry conditions \nwithin the forecast area today. A few showers may edge into the\narea, mainly along and west of the Ohio River, as high pressure\nretreats east and the shortwave passes overhead tonight into \nMonday. \n\nThe next opportunity for precipitation arrives when an upper \ntrough and associated systems pivot into the Middle Ohio Valley \nmid to late week. Discrepancies in forecast models lead to low\nconfidence in precipitation amounts and the timing of the \nsystems.\n\nTemperatures will remain above normal though at least the \nmiddle of the week. Cooler air transported down into the area \nby the aforementioned upper trough should allow temperatures to\nbecome more seasonable for the end of the week.",
